## About this package

This is a time-series forecasting package: a model trained on historical
values of one or more related series, producing probabilistic forecasts over
a horizon of future steps. The package's central entry point:

```
forecast(model, history, static_features, time_varying_features, graph,
         entity_ids, target_scaling_state, seed,
         *paradigm_extras_by_name) -> ForecastResult
```

`ForecastResult` carries the forecast mean, an uncertainty estimate, Monte
Carlo samples from the forecast distribution, and the raw distribution
parameters. Methods without relational structure between series pass
`graph=None`. `entity_ids` names the series axis with typed stable identities;
`target_scaling_state` is the training-only fitted state keyed by those
identities. The function restores every target-valued result field to original
target units before returning it and never joins scale state by row position.
It uses the fixed `method.target_scaling.inverse_forecast_output` helper for
the `location`, `samples`, `distribution_scale`, and `variance` roles;
dimensionless shape parameters stay unchanged.

`train_model` also returns one canonical `training_history` record created by
the fixed `method.training_history.record_training_history` helper. It binds
ordered finite losses and any single-holdout selection to the exact fitting
and selection ranges, seed, configuration id, scaling-state id, model id, and
checkpoint id. The generated package returns and may print this record; only
the R2C pipeline writes the durable `.pipeline/training_history.json` artifact.

