## Quick start

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
jupyter notebook notebook.ipynb
```

Click **Run All**. The notebook trains at demonstration scale, produces
forecasts on a held-out window, evaluates them against naive baselines
(predict-zero and repeat-last-value), emits one structured
`R2C_DEMO_EVALUATION_JSON:` record from the executed evaluation objects, and
prints a deterministic `Demo verdict:` presentation line derived from that
record. The structured record — joined by the pipeline to its split-validity
receipt — is the evidence authority; the prose line is not.
It carries the model and comparator metrics beside the exact predictions; the
pipeline recomputes each metric and requires numerical agreement.
The record identities use `sha256:` plus SHA-256 over compact, sorted-key
UTF-8 JSON with no NaN tokens: `{actuals, row_ids, units}` for actual values
and `{finite_mask, row_ids}` for the mask. Masked missing values are JSON
`null`.
The finite mask is exactly the finiteness of the executed actuals; it cannot
exclude finite rows according to model or baseline performance. Repeat-last
inputs all come from the final position immediately before the complete
evaluation window, so a later horizon never reads an earlier held-out actual
or an arbitrarily older weak value.

